Notebook[{
Cell["Graphical calculus \:00a73.3.1\:20133.3.3: twists and ribbon categories", "Title"],
Cell["Turaev & Virelizier, Monoidal Categories and Topological Field Theory, pp. 59\:201362 \:00b7 sections 60\:201365 \:00b7 continues the notebooks for \:00a72.1\:20133.2", "Subtitle"],
Cell["By Dara O Shayda and Noor Hoshino (\:661f\:91ce\:30cc\:30fc\:30eb)", "Text"],
Cell["59. Setup", "Section"],
Cell["The first cell loads the engine from this folder (Desktop/Research/Monoidal Graphical Calculus). The code of this notebook is also saved on its own as ribbon-3.3.wl, which the GraphicalCalculusKernel loads.", "Text"],
Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n(* the engine: sections 0\:201319, 20\:201327, 30\:201335, 40\:201347 and 50\:201355, all in this folder *)\ndir = FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"Desktop\", \"Research\", \"Monoidal Graphical Calculus\"}];\nWith[{cells = Cases[Get[FileNameJoin[{dir, \"graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb\"}]], Cell[c_, \"Input\" | \"Code\", ___] :> c, Infinity]},\n Scan[Quiet@Check[TimeConstrained[ToExpression[#, StandardForm]; Null, 120], Null] &, cells];\n Print[\"Loaded \", Length[cells], \" code cells from graphical-calculus-2.1-simplify.nb\"]];\ndir = FileNameJoin[{$HomeDirectory, \"Desktop\", \"Research\", \"Monoidal Graphical Calculus\"}];\nQuiet[Get[FileNameJoin[{dir, #}]]] & /@ {\"pivotal-2.1.3.wl\", \"penrose-2.2.wl\", \"pivotal-2.3-2.7.wl\", \"braided-2.7-3.2.wl\"};\nPrint[\"Loaded pivotal-2.1.3.wl, penrose-2.2.wl, pivotal-2.3-2.7.wl and braided-2.7-3.2.wl\"];", "Input"],
Cell["60. \:00a73.3.1 Twists: the curls \:03b8\:02e1_X, \:03b8\:02b3_X and their inverses", "Section"],
Cell["\:03b8\:02e1_X = (ev_X \:2297 id_X)(id_X* \:2297 \:03c4_X,X)(c\:0303oev_X \:2297 id_X) and \:03b8\:02b3_X = (id_X \:2297 \:1ebdv_X)(\:03c4_X,X \:2297 id_X* )(id_X \:2297 coev_X) are curls on the strand X.\n   By Lemma 3.2 their inverses are the curls with the other crossing:\n   (\:03b8\:02e1_X)\:207b\:00b9 = (id_X \:2297 \:1ebdv_X)(\:03c4\:207b\:00b9_X,X \:2297 id_X* )(id_X \:2297 coev_X) and (\:03b8\:02b3_X)\:207b\:00b9 = (ev_X \:2297 id_X)(id_X* \:2297 \:03c4\:207b\:00b9_X,X)(c\:0303oev_X \:2297 id_X).\n   \"twist fold\" recognises the four curls, in three consecutive layers, and replaces each by a box \:03b8\:02e1_X, \:03b8\:02b3_X, \:03b8\:02e1\:207b\:00b9_X or \:03b8\:02b3\:207b\:00b9_X.", "Text"],
Cell["thetaL[x_] := Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\", x];  thetaR[x_] := Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\", x];\nthetaLInv[x_] := Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\\:207b\\:00b9\", x];  thetaRInv[x_] := Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\\:207b\\:00b9\", x];\ntwistQ[s_] := MatchQ[s, Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\" | \"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\" | \"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\\:207b\\:00b9\" | \"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\\:207b\\:00b9\", _String]];\ntwistB[t_, x_] := B[t[x], partsU[x], partsU[x]];\n\n(* the curls, as layered diagrams on a strand coloured x *)\ncurlL[x_, pos_] := LD[{x}, {{0, B[coevR[x], {}, {star[x], x}]}, {1, crossingB[pos, {x, x}]}, {0, B[evL[x], {star[x], x}, {}]}}];   (* \:03b8\:02e1, or (\:03b8\:02b3)\:207b\:00b9 *)\ncurlR[x_, pos_] := LD[{x}, {{1, B[coevL[x], {}, {x, star[x]}]}, {0, crossingB[pos, {x, x}]}, {1, B[evR[x], {x, star[x]}, {}]}}];   (* \:03b8\:02b3, or (\:03b8\:02e1)\:207b\:00b9 *)\nthetaLDef[x_] := curlL[x, True];  thetaRInvDef[x_] := curlL[x, False];\nthetaRDef[x_] := curlR[x, True];  thetaLInvDef[x_] := curlR[x, False];\n\n(* The three layers of a curl need not be consecutive: layers between them that do not touch the curl's three strands are allowed (level exchange).\n   For each cup in turn, the window w..w+2 of the curl's strands is followed up the diagram; the first complete curl is folded,\n   and the twist box takes the place of the crossing. *)\ntwistFold[ld : LD[src_, ls_]] := Module[{rs = rows[ld], n = Length[ls]},\n   Catch[Do[Module[{a = ls[[i, 1]], b = ls[[i, 2]], type = None, x, w, w0, stage = 1, sg, jj, wj, right = {}, tp, ep, lo, hi},\n      Which[MatchQ[sym[b], Subscript[OverTilde[\"coev\"], _String]] && Length[outs[b]] == 2, type = \"L\"; w = a,\n       MatchQ[sym[b], Subscript[\"coev\", _String]] && Length[outs[b]] == 2 && a >= 1, type = \"R\"; w = a - 1];\n      lo[] := If[stage == 2 && type == \"R\", w + 1, w]; hi[] := If[stage == 2 && type == \"L\", w + 1, w + 2];\n      If[type =!= None && Length[rs[[i]]] > w && rs[[i, w + 1]] === sym[b][[2]],\n       x = sym[b][[2]];\n       Do[With[{p = ls[[j, 1]], bb = ls[[j, 2]]}, With[{ni = Length[ins[bb]], no = Length[outs[bb]]},\n          tp = If[type == \"L\", w + 1, w]; ep = If[type == \"L\", w, w + 1];\n          Which[\n           stage == 1 && p == tp && tauQ[sym[bb]] && ins[bb] === {x, x}, sg = tauPos[sym[bb]]; jj = j; wj = w; stage = 2,\n           (* a one-line box on the incoming strand, before the crossing, stays below the twist *)\n           stage == 1 && ni == 1 && no == 1 && p == If[type == \"L\", w + 2, w], If[type == \"L\", AppendTo[right, j]],\n           stage == 2 && p == ep && ni == 2 && sym[bb] === If[type == \"L\", Subscript[\"ev\", x], Subscript[OverTilde[\"ev\"], x]],\n            Throw[LD[src, Table[Which[k == jj, {wj, twistB[Which[type == \"L\" && sg, thetaL, type == \"L\", thetaRInv, sg, thetaR, True, thetaLInv], x]},\n                 MemberQ[right, k], {ls[[k, 1]] - 2, ls[[k, 2]]}, True, ls[[k]]], {k, Complement[Range[n], {i, j}]}]]],\n           (* outside the strands still in use: all three before the crossing; after it, the curl's outgoing strand is free *)\n           If[ni == 0, p <= lo[], p + ni - 1 < lo[]], w += no - ni,\n           p > hi[], AppendTo[right, j],\n           True, Break[]]]], {j, i + 1, n}]]], {i, n}]; $Failed]];", "Input"],
Cell["61. Lemma 3.2 and \:00a73.3.2: the rules for twists", "Section"],
Cell["twists and their inverses cancel; a twist slides down through a one-line box (naturality, Lemma 3.2);\n   on a tensor product it is Exercise 3.3.3, \:03b8_X\:2297Y = (\:03b8_X \:2297 \:03b8_Y) \:03c4_Y,X \:03c4_X,Y, and \:03b8_\|01d7d9 = id_\|01d7d9.\n   A ribbon category (\:00a73.3.2) has \:03b8\:02e1 = \:03b8\:02b3; \"ribbon\" writes every \:03b8\:02b3 as \:03b8\:02e1.", "Text"],
Cell["twistInvQ[s1_, s2_] := MatchQ[{s1, s2},\n   {Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\", x_], Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\\:207b\\:00b9\", x_]} | {Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\\:207b\\:00b9\", x_], Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\", x_]} |\n   {Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\", x_], Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\\:207b\\:00b9\", x_]} | {Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\\:207b\\:00b9\", x_], Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\", x_]}];\ncancelTwist[{a_, B[s1_, {c_}, {c_}]}, {a_, B[s2_, {c_}, {c_}]}] /; twistInvQ[s1, s2] := {};\ncancelTwist[__] := $Failed;\nnaturalTwist[{a_, B[f_String, {x_}, {y_}]}, {a_, B[Subscript[h_, y_], {y_}, {y_}]}] /; twistQ[Subscript[h, y]] :=\n  {{a, B[Subscript[h, x], {x}, {x}]}, {a, B[f, {x}, {y}]}};\nnaturalTwist[__] := $Failed;\ntwistTensor[{a_, B[Subscript[h_, x_String], i_, i_]}] /; twistQ[Subscript[h, x]] := With[{ps = partsU[x]},\n   Which[ps === {}, {},\n    Length[ps] > 1 && (h === \"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\" || h === \"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\"),\n     With[{p = First[ps], r = joinParts[Rest[ps]]},\n      {{a, tauB[p, r]}, {a, tauB[r, p]}, {a, B[Subscript[h, p], {p}, {p}]}, {a + 1, B[Subscript[h, r], partsU[r], partsU[r]]}}],\n    True, $Failed]];\ntwistTensor[_] := $Failed;\nribbonTwist[{a_, B[Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\", x_], i_, o_]}] := {{a, B[Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\", x], i, o]}};\nribbonTwist[{a_, B[Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\\:207b\\:00b9\", x_], i_, o_]}] := {{a, B[Subscript[\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\\:207b\\:00b9\", x], i, o]}};\nribbonTwist[_] := $Failed;\n\ntwistRules = <|\n   \"twist fold (\\[Section]3.3.1)\" -> {\"ld\", twistFold},\n   \"twists cancel (Lemma 3.2)\" -> {2, cancelTwist},\n   \"naturality of \\[Theta] (Lemma 3.2)\" -> {2, naturalTwist},\n   \"twist on \\[CircleTimes] (Exercise 3.3.3)\" -> {1, twistTensor}|>;\nribbonRules = <|\"ribbon: \\[Theta]\\:02b3 = \\[Theta]\\:02e1 (\\[Section]3.3.2)\" -> {1, ribbonTwist}|>;\n\n(* the fold goes in before Lemma 2.3, so that a curl on an upward strand is recognised before its cap and cup are rewritten *)\nwithTwists[rs_Association] := With[{k = Keys[rs], i = First[FirstPosition[Keys[rs], \"Lemma 2.3 (X** = X)\"]]},\n   Join[AssociationThread[Take[k, i - 1], Lookup[rs, Take[k, i - 1]]], KeyTake[twistRules, {\"twist fold (\\[Section]3.3.1)\"}],\n    AssociationThread[Drop[k, i - 1], Lookup[rs, Drop[k, i - 1]]], KeyDrop[twistRules, {\"twist fold (\\[Section]3.3.1)\"}]]];\nrulesTw = withTwists[rulesDB];                               (* braided pivotal *)\nrulesRib = Join[withTwists[rulesSB], ribbonRules];           (* ribbon; spherical by Corollary 3.4 *)", "Input"],
Cell["62. A matrix model with twists: graded vector spaces with a bicharacter and weights", "Section"],
Cell["Colours are graded (grade g, braiding q^(g h) \:00b7 flip) and weighted (\:1ebdv_X = w(X)\:00b7pairing, c\:0303oev_X = pairing/w(X)); boxes keep grade and weight.\n   Then \:03b8\:02e1_X = q^(g\:00b2)/w(X)\:00b7id and \:03b8\:02b3_X = q^(g\:00b2) w(X)\:00b7id, so the category is ribbon exactly when w(X)\:00b2 = 1 for every X; with w = 1 it is ribbon with twist q^(g\:00b2).\n   Lemma 3.5's pivotal structure \:1ebdv_X = ev_X \:03c4_X,X* is the weight w(X) = q^(\:2212g\:00b2), a character only when q^(2gh) = 1, that is, for a symmetry.", "Text"],
Cell["matGW[ld_LD, n_, gr_, q_, w_, mats_] := Module[{rs = rows[ld], m, dimC, box},\n   dimC[cs_List] := Times @@ (nOf[#, n] & /@ cs);\n   box[b_B] := With[{s = sym[b]},\n     Which[\n      tauQ[s] && Length[ins[b]] == 2,\n       With[{l = ins[b][[1]], r = ins[b][[2]]},\n        If[tauPos[s], q^(gradeOf[l, gr] gradeOf[r, gr]), q^(-gradeOf[l, gr] gradeOf[r, gr])] flipM[nOf[l, n], nOf[r, n]]],\n      tauQ[s], matGW[LD[ins[b], braidSplit[{0, b}]], n, gr, q, w, mats],\n      twistQ[s] && Length[ins[b]] == 1, With[{x = s[[2]]},\n        matGW[Switch[s[[1]], \"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\", thetaLDef[x], \"\\[Theta]\\:02b3\", thetaRDef[x], \"\\[Theta]\\:02e1\\:207b\\:00b9\", thetaLInvDef[x], _, thetaRInvDef[x]], n, gr, q, w, mats]],\n      twistQ[s], matGW[LD[ins[b], twistTensor[{0, b}]], n, gr, q, w, mats],\n      True, matBox[b, n, w, mats]]];\n   m = IdentityMatrix[dimC[First[rs]]];\n   Do[With[{a = ld[[2, k, 1]], b = ld[[2, k, 2]], row = rs[[k]]},\n     m = KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[dimC[Take[row, a]]], box[b], IdentityMatrix[dimC[Drop[row, a + Length[ins[b]]]]]] . m], {k, Length[ld[[2]]]}];\n   m];", "Input"],
Cell["63. The constructions of pp. 59\:201362, as layered diagrams", "Section"],
Cell["SeedRandom[3303];\nnT = (2 &);  grT = <|\"X\" -> 1, \"Y\" -> 2, \"Z\" -> 1|>;  qT = 3;\nwBraided = <|\"X\" -> 2, \"Y\" -> 2, \"Z\" -> 2|>;          (* braided pivotal, not ribbon *)\nwRibbon = <|\"X\" -> 1, \"Y\" -> -1, \"Z\" -> 1|>;          (* ribbon *)\nmatsT = <|\"f\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}], \"g\" -> RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {2, 2}]|>;\nmT[ld_, w_: wBraided, q_: qT, gr_: grT] := matGW[ld, nT, gr, q, w, matsT];\ninT[{l__}, w_: wBraided, q_: qT, gr_: grT] := Equal @@ (mT[#, w, q, gr] & /@ {l});\nboxT[t_, x_] := LD[partsU[x], {{0, twistB[t, x]}}];\n\nlem32 = <|\n   \"the curl is \\[Theta]\\:02e1_X\" -> {thetaLDef[\"X\"], boxT[thetaL, \"X\"]},\n   \"\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X (\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X)\\:207b\\:00b9 = id (the curls of Lemma 3.2)\" -> {stackL[thetaLInvDef[\"X\"], thetaLDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X\"}]},\n   \"(\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X)\\:207b\\:00b9 \\[Theta]\\:02e1_X = id\" -> {stackL[thetaLDef[\"X\"], thetaLInvDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X\"}]},\n   \"\\[Theta]\\:02b3_X (\\[Theta]\\:02b3_X)\\:207b\\:00b9 = id\" -> {stackL[thetaRInvDef[\"X\"], thetaRDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X\"}]},\n   \"naturality: \\[Theta]\\:02e1_Z f = f \\[Theta]\\:02e1_X\" -> {stackL[boxL[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"Z\"}], boxT[thetaL, \"Z\"]], stackL[boxT[thetaL, \"X\"], boxL[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"Z\"}]]},\n   \"naturality: \\[Theta]\\:02b3_Z f = f \\[Theta]\\:02b3_X\" -> {stackL[boxL[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"Z\"}], thetaRDef[\"Z\"]], stackL[thetaRDef[\"X\"], boxL[\"f\", {\"X\"}, {\"Z\"}]]},\n   \"a curl on an upward strand is \\[Theta]\\:02e1_X*\" -> {thetaLDef[\"X*\"], boxT[thetaL, \"X*\"]}|>;\n(* matrix-only parts of Lemma 3.2 and (3.4): duals of twists and traces of twists *)\nlem32m = <|\n   \"(\\[Theta]\\:02b3_X)* = \\[Theta]\\:02e1_X*\" -> {dualLD[thetaRDef[\"X\"]], thetaLDef[\"X*\"]},\n   \"(\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X)* = \\[Theta]\\:02b3_X*\" -> {dualLD[thetaLDef[\"X\"]], thetaRDef[\"X*\"]},\n   \"(3.4) tr_r(\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X) = tr_l(\\[Theta]\\:02b3_X)\" -> {trR[thetaLDef[\"X\"]], trL[thetaRDef[\"X\"]]}|>;\nex333 = <|\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X\\[CircleTimes]Y = (\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X \\[CircleTimes] \\[Theta]\\:02e1_Y) \\[Tau]_Y,X \\[Tau]_X,Y\" -> {boxT[thetaL, \"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\"],\n      stackL[LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {0, tauB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}], besideL[boxT[thetaL, \"X\"], boxT[thetaL, \"Y\"]]]},\n    \"\\[Theta]\\:02b3_X\\[CircleTimes]Y = (\\[Theta]\\:02b3_X \\[CircleTimes] \\[Theta]\\:02b3_Y) \\[Tau]_Y,X \\[Tau]_X,Y\" -> {boxT[thetaR, \"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\"],\n      stackL[LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"Y\"]}, {0, tauB[\"Y\", \"X\"]}}], besideL[boxT[thetaR, \"X\"], boxT[thetaR, \"Y\"]]]}|>;\n(* the curl picture of \:03b8_X\:2297Y, written out with tensor caps: checked in matrices *)\nthetaLXY = LD[{\"X\", \"Y\"}, {{0, B[coevR[\"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\"], {}, {\"Y*\", \"X*\", \"X\", \"Y\"}]}, {2, tauB[\"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\", \"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\"]},\n     {0, B[evL[\"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\"], {\"Y*\", \"X*\", \"X\", \"Y\"}, {}]}}];\n(* \:00a73.3.2 ribbon categories, Theorem 3.3, Corollary 3.4 *)\nrib = <|\"ribbon: \\[Theta]\\:02e1_X = \\[Theta]\\:02b3_X\" -> {thetaLDef[\"X\"], thetaRDef[\"X\"]},\n    \"Theorem 3.3, R1: the double curl \\[Theta]\\:02b3_X (\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X)\\:207b\\:00b9 is id_X\" -> {stackL[thetaLInvDef[\"X\"], thetaRDef[\"X\"]], idL[{\"X\"}]},\n    \"Theorem 3.3, R1 on an upward strand\" -> {stackL[thetaLInvDef[\"X*\"], thetaRDef[\"X*\"]], idL[{\"X*\"}]}|>;\nribm = <|\"self-dual twist: (\\[Theta]_X)* = \\[Theta]_X*\" -> {dualLD[thetaLDef[\"X\"]], thetaLDef[\"X*\"]}|>;\ncor34 = <|\"Corollary 3.4: tr_l(f) = tr_r(f)\" -> {trL[boxL[\"g\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]], trR[boxL[\"g\", {\"X\"}, {\"X\"}]]}|>;\n(* Lemma 3.5: a symmetry and \:1ebdv_X = ev_X \:03c4_X,X* give a ribbon category with twist id; super vector spaces *)\nwLemma35[gr_, q_] := (q^(-gr[#]^2) &);\nlem35 = <|\"\\[Theta]\\:02e1_X = id\" -> {thetaLDef[\"X\"], idL[{\"X\"}]}, \"\\[Theta]\\:02b3_X = id\" -> {thetaRDef[\"X\"], idL[{\"X\"}]},\n    \"\\:1ebdv_X = ev_X \\[Tau]_X,X*\" -> {LD[{\"X\", \"X*\"}, {{0, B[evR[\"X\"], {\"X\", \"X*\"}, {}]}}], LD[{\"X\", \"X*\"}, {{0, tauB[\"X\", \"X*\"]}, {0, B[evL[\"X\"], {\"X*\", \"X\"}, {}]}}]}|>;\n(* Lemma 3.6: tr(f) = \:03c9(f \:2297 id_Y) P(\:2217\:03c9) for a non-degenerate pairing \:03c9 : X \:2297 Y \:2192 k *)\nlemma36[] := Module[{n = 3, M, f, g, om, contr, P},\n   M = RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {n, n}]; While[Det[M] == 0, M = RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {n, n}]];\n   f = RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {n, n}]; g = RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, {n, n}];\n   om = Flatten[M];                                   (* \:03c9(x \:2297 y) = x\:1d40 M y *)\n   contr = Flatten[Inverse[M]];                       (* \:2217\:03c9 \:2208 Y \:2297 X, the inverse of \:03c9 *)\n   P = flipM[n, n];                                    (* Y \:2297 X \:2192 X \:2297 Y *)\n   {om . KroneckerProduct[f, IdentityMatrix[n]] . P . contr == Tr[f], om . KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[n], g] . P . contr == Tr[g],\n    om . P . contr == Tr[IdentityMatrix[n]]}];", "Input"],
Cell["64. Checking", "Section"],
Cell["byRulesT[{l__}, rs_: rulesTw] := SameQ @@ (simplifyLD[#, rs] & /@ {l});\nstepsKeepT[ld_, rs_: rulesTw, w_: wBraided] := Equal @@ (mT[#[[2]], w] & /@ simplifyTrace[ld, rs]);", "Input"],
Cell["64a. Walkthrough", "Section"],
Cell["\:00a73.3.1 curls become twists", "Subsection"],
Cell["Two curls drawn out, \:03b8\:02e1_X after (\:03b8\:02e1_X)\:207b\:00b9. The first fold finds the curl with \:03c4\:207b\:00b9 even though the layers of the other curl sit between its three layers; then the twists cancel (Lemma 3.2):", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[lem32[[2, 1]], rulesTw]]", "Input"],
Cell["In the model of section 62 (q = 3, grade 1, weight 2) \:03b8\:02e1_X = q/w \:00b7 id and \:03b8\:02b3_X = q w \:00b7 id:", "Text"],
Cell["{mT[boxT[thetaL, \"X\"]], mT[boxT[thetaR, \"X\"]]}", "Input"],
Cell["Lemma 3.2 naturality", "Subsection"],
Cell["The curl \:03b8\:02b3_Z drawn above f is folded, then slides below f:", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[lem32[[6, 1]], rulesTw]]", "Input"],
Cell["Exercise 3.3.3", "Subsection"],
Cell["The twist of X \:2297 Y is the double crossing followed by the twists of X and Y:", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[ex333[[1, 1]], rulesTw]]", "Input"],
Cell["Theorem 3.3 and Corollary 3.4", "Subsection"],
Cell["In a ribbon category the double curl \:03b8\:02b3_X (\:03b8\:02e1_X)\:207b\:00b9 (R1) is the identity: the folds, \:03b8\:02b3 = \:03b8\:02e1, and the cancellation:", "Text"],
Cell["showTraceP[simplifyTrace[rib[[2, 1]], rulesRib]]", "Input"],
Cell["Corollary 3.4: tr_l(g) = tr_r(g) holds in the ribbon model (w = \:00b11) and fails for w = 2:", "Text"],
Cell["{inT[cor34[[1]], wRibbon], inT[cor34[[1]], wBraided]}", "Input"],
Cell["65. Tests", "Section"],
Cell["Each identity is checked by the rules and in the model of section 62: graded vector spaces with braiding q^(g h) \:00b7 flip, q = 3, and weights w. For w = 2 the category is braided pivotal but not ribbon; for w = \:00b11 it is ribbon.", "Text"],
Cell["grS3 = <|\"X\" -> 1, \"Y\" -> 0|>;\n<|\n \"Lemma 3.2 by the rules (rulesTw)\" -> AllTrue[Values[lem32], byRulesT],\n \"Lemma 3.2 in the model (q = 3, w = 2)\" -> AllTrue[Values[lem32], inT],\n \"Lemma 3.2: (\:03b8\:02b3_X)* = \:03b8\:02e1_X*, (\:03b8\:02e1_X)* = \:03b8\:02b3_X* and (3.4), in the model\" -> AllTrue[Values[lem32m], inT],\n \"Exercise 3.3.3 by the rules and in the model, also with tensor caps\" -> (AllTrue[Values[ex333], byRulesT] && AllTrue[Values[ex333], inT] && inT[{thetaLXY, boxT[thetaL, \"X\\[CircleTimes]Y\"]}]),\n \"every step keeps the matrix\" -> AllTrue[Flatten[Values[Join[lem32, ex333]], 1], stepsKeepT],\n \"not ribbon for w = 2: the ribbon identities fail by rules and matrices\" -> (NoneTrue[Values[rib], byRulesT] && NoneTrue[Values[rib], inT]),\n \"ribbon for w = \\[PlusMinus]1: \:00a73.3.2 and Theorem 3.3 by rulesRib and matrices\" -> (AllTrue[Values[rib], byRulesT[#, rulesRib] &] && AllTrue[Values[Join[rib, ribm]], inT[#, wRibbon] &] &&\n     AllTrue[Flatten[Values[rib], 1], stepsKeepT[#, rulesRib, wRibbon] &]),\n \"Corollary 3.4: ribbon \\[Implies] spherical\" -> (byRulesT[cor34[[1]], rulesRib] && inT[cor34[[1]], wRibbon] && ! inT[cor34[[1]], wBraided]),\n \"Lemma 3.5: super vector spaces with \\:1ebdv_X = ev_X \\[Tau]_X,X* are ribbon with \\[Theta] = id\" -> AllTrue[Values[lem35], inT[#, wLemma35[grS3, -1], -1, grS3] &],\n \"Lemma 3.5 needs a symmetry: for q = 3 the same pivotal structure gives \\[Theta] \\[NotEqual] id\" -> ! inT[lem35[[1]], wLemma35[grT, 3], 3],\n \"Lemma 3.6: tr(f) = \\[Omega](f \\[CircleTimes] id) P (\\[Star]\\[Omega])\" -> (And @@ lemma36[]),\n \"earlier results unchanged under rulesTw\" -> (AllTrue[Values[Join[br, rm]], byRulesB[#, rulesTw] &] && byRulesB[lem210[[1]], rulesTw])\n|>", "Input"],
Cell["Appendix: what is and is not mechanised", "Section"],
Cell["The dual statements of Lemma 3.2, (\:03b8\:02b3_X)* = \:03b8\:02e1_X* and (\:03b8\:02e1_X)* = \:03b8\:02b3_X*, and (3.4) are checked in matrices only: the fold rules of \:00a72.1.3 do not see twist boxes.", "Item"],
Cell["Theorem 3.3 is checked for R1 on downward and upward strands; the full statement (invariance of the ribbon-graph evaluation) is not mechanised.", "Item"],
Cell["Lemma 3.5 is checked for super vector spaces; the independence of traces from the chosen dual and Lemma 3.6 are checked numerically for random pairings.", "Item"],
Cell["The twist fold accepts layers between a curl's three layers when they do not touch its strands, and a one-line box on the incoming strand before the crossing.", "Item"],
Cell["\:00a9 Computational Classnotes \:00b7 CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "Text"]
}, StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
